  "notes": "The prayer said with hands spread over the offerings, and the point at which, by universal custom rather than by rubric, the server's bell announces the approaching consecration. Its second half is the addition the Liber Pontificalis credits to Gregory the Great. PLACÁTUS at w014 is tagged as the adjective, with both analyzers, rather than as a participle of placo; it agrees with the subject of accípias, so the sense is that God receives the offering already appeased. ÉRIPI at w027 and NUMERÁRI at w034 are present passive infinitives depending on iúbeas; the two clauses share that one verb across a long separation.",
